---
date: 2026-06-05T16:40:21-04:00
---

@timeline
{
- {Prehistory} The world is mundane. No magic permeates the air, and no worlds are seen in the night sky.
- {Before 0ag} A crack appears in the firmament, and magic floods into [[Færrin]]. Warlords obtain this magic and subjugate the populace, beginning the Dark Ages.
- {0ag} The [[Iridescent Host]] instructs the Hierophant Aurelia to widen the crack, allowing divine blessings to pass through and ending the Dark Ages.
- {0ag - 12ag} Aurelia and her companions wage holy war against the Warlords of [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]], eventually ending their rule and bringing about the modern age.
- {41ag} Aurelia is granted a gift for her new church, the secrets of creating divine life. She calls this new life a [[Hearts|Heart]]. The first Heart, Rule of Three, is born within the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]].
- {48ag} Helm and Torun Karavi, two of Aurelia's companions, leave her side to found [[Belvedere]] on the peaks of [[Geography/Austrene/index|Austrene]].
- {51ag} Culoum Honor-Sworn, another of Aurelia's companions, takes up residence in the Opaline Mountains. He brings a contingent of knights and mages, who would become the first council of [[Org/The Scale/index|The Scale]].
- {76ag} Harrier Rael, the last of Aurelia's original companions, leaves on a trek across Edan to find the meaning behind her life.
- {80ag} Harrier Rael ends her journey in the Evergreen Delta, and founds [[Geography/Raelion/index|Raelion]].
- {101ag} Aurelia passes away. Calaria mourns for a month.
- {101ag} Aurelia II is born on the 30th day of mourning. Her birth is heralded by divine revelations across the continent. The Church rejoices the return of their pontifex.
- {148ag} Obie Toombs, a scavenger in [[Geography/Istria/index|Istria]], accidentally creates the first slide and discovers the [[Infinite Horizon]].
- {156ag} Parmann Chorath integrates his friend Obie's slide into a horse-drawn carriage, calling it a "Slider".
- {159ag} Obie and Parmann lead a convoy starward into the Horizon. The convoy is never seen again.
- {212ag} Aurthalaxus the Plaguebearer is empowered by the [[Heir of the Plague|Heir]] to cull life on Edan.
- {228ag} Aurthalaxus wipes out his home country of Fūlwinter, and crosses the Tenchwin for his next target -- the Siksithys Kingdom.
- {234ag} The Siksithys Kingdom's lands are salted and its buildings razed, reducing the vibrant forest kingdom to a lifeless desert. Aurthalaxus marches on Calaria.
- {236ag} Aurelia II is slain in combat against Aurthalaxus, but the Plaguebearer is hurt and retreats to mend his wounds.
- {254ag} Aurelia III, trained from birth, slays Aurthalaxus amidst the ruined cities of Siksithys. The continent rejoices.
- {271ag} New settlements being to crop up in the remains of Fūlwinter. Its people are regarded with distrust, due to the Plaguebearer's actions. With their reputation already so low, many turn to piracy.
- {302ag} Istrian settlers migrate north in search of an escape from the [[Stillness]]. They find the mineral-rich [[Geography/Velthara/index|Velthara]], and settle there to begin extracting the ground's bounty.
- {361ag} Aurelia III passes. Aurelia IV is born in a small fishing settlement in [[Geography/Fenrith/index|Fenrith]]. When the Iridescent Church appears to bring Aurelia IV into the fold, her parents refuse to give her up. The Church takes her by force.
- {362ag} Arkon of the Mist rallies the villages of Fenrith against the Church, and becomes the first Fisher-King. The people begin the long march across the Termean Veinlands.
- {362ag} Arkon of the Mist befriends Clan Tyrlock of Istria and Parfus Tormeré. They march together towards Calaria to retrieve Aurelia IV.
- {364ag} Arkon of the Mist and his convoy arrive at Hallia. Aurelia IV declares that she wishes to stay in Calaria, shocking the convoy. Arkon swears to stay until Aurelia can be cured of her brainwashing.
- {368ag} After years of waiting outside the city limits, the convoy disperses. Aurelia IV remains in Hallia, and the Fisher-King returns, defeated, to Fenrith.
- {436ag} Forster Cain founds [[Org/Prime Meridian/index|Prime Meridian]], the first modern [[Org/index|Org]]. Cain is granted the right to manage roads in outer settlements of Calaria by the royal family.
- {475ag} Aurelia IV passes. Aurelia V is born in [[Geography/Tormeré/index|Tormeré]], where she is joyfully raised by the local church.
- {481ag} Orber Chorath finds his ancestor's designs for a Slider and builds a prototype with an internal combustion engine. His invention would become the basis for [[Chorath Engineering]].
- {500ag} The Quincentenary of the Gods is celebrated across the continent. Forster Cain marks the occasion by unveiling the first train in Hallia.
- {514ag} Prime Meridian officially takes over the infrastructural needs of Calaria. All roads, rail stations, and tramways are managed by the Org.
- {515ag} Forster Cain and Aurelia V perform a bloodless coup in Calaria. The royal family is deposed and a unified council of Orgs and the Iridescent Church take control.
- {591ag} Aurelia V collapses during a speech on the anniversary of the death of Aurthalaxus. Many suspect foul play, but the Church gives no confirmations.
- {599ag} Aurelia V is pronounced dead, after years of attempted medical intervention. Aurelia VI is born in the slums of Belwick, the capital of the Calarian province of [[Geography/Brithwyn/index|Brithwyn]]. The local populace are proud to be host to the next Pontifex.
- {620ag} Aurelia VI declares that she will not leave her people after a mere century of service, and promise to devote her protection and leadership to the Church for time everlasting.
- {699ag} A century-old Aurelia VI announces that she has received another boon from the Host, and will live eternally. Lookers-on later say that she didn't look a day over 30 during her address.
- {724ag} The [[Godhome|Twin Suns]] disappear from the sky for nearly a month. Researchers in Belvedere confirm this is a rebound from excessive augury. Aurelia VI accuses Raelion, which Raelion vehemently denies. Calaria breaks a longstanding trade deal with Raelion in response. The event becomes known as the Incident of 24, and is the first crack in the relationship between the two countries, which would eventually devolve into war. Whether Raelion was doing it, whether it was a Calarian false flag, or whether a third party was responsible is still debated; it is taught in Calarian schools that Raelion was responsible.
- {792ag} At 193 years old, the divine magic sustaining Aurelia VI fails and she passes away. Aurelia VII is found left on a doorstep of an orphanage in Hallia. The Cardinal Prime of Brithwyn declares that they received no such divine revelation about Aurelia VII's birth, and a rift forms between them and the Calarian church.
- {802ag} The prime minister of Calaria is assassinated during a ceremony in the Imperial Graveyard. The assassins enchanted a statue of Aurelia I to kill him during a speech. The killers are never caught.
- {802ag} In the chaos of the the assassination, Brithwyn declares its independence from the rest of Calaria, citing that the Church has lost its way. The Calarian Church sends troops to Brithwyn to bring them back in line.
- {803ag} The Org council elects Rhys Lawson to be the new prime minister of Calaria. Lawson runs on a platform of vengeance, claiming the assassination to be perpetrated by Raelion. The Raelish government denies the allegations.
- {803ag} Prime Minister Lawson declares war on Raelion, beginning an offensive on two fronts for Calaria. The Iridescent Church of Calaria endorses Lawson's war, dubbing it a holy war.
- {812ag} Prime Minister Lawson recalls troops from Brithwyn, and promises to recognize their independence, on the condition that they aid in the conflict against Raelion. Brithwyn accepts.
- {823ag} Calaria ends the war with Raelion on the Night of the Midnight Sun. An explosive causes a chain reaction across the weave of Raelion, sundering the nation and leaving a gaping magic wound in the earth in its place.
- {858ag} The [[Voidsong]] is first heard in Calaria. Scholars across the continent debate its importance and meaning.
- {862ag} A wall of fire surrounds the district of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]] in Hallia. Attempts to reclaim it by the Calarian government fail, and an accord is reached between the Church and [[Org/Pyrelight/index|Pyrelight]]. Teller's Run is declared a sovereign city-state.
- {863ag} Months before the Party joins [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]], three Undercrofters of the strider city [[Geography/Istria/Iomenei|Iomenei]] are offered a place on the upper decks to find the saboteur who froze two of the city's legs. They trace the sabotage to the elven fluid master [[People/Gerhard|Gerhard]], who bears the face and horn mark of [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]], and clear a hive of insects from a forsaken sector below.
- {863ag} The Party joins [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]].
- {863ag} The Party takes a courier job from [[Copperjaw]] at [[Org/Sableclutch Scrap/index|Sableclutch Scrap]], carrying a locked case across [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] toward the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Diamond District/index|Diamond District]].
- {863ag} Two [[Ugathal]] wearing the shapes of men ambush the Party in a [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] alley for the case they carry, and are killed. Badges that look genuine are found lodged inside their flesh.
- {863ag} The Scale delvers reopen the fountain of blood in [[Geography/The Quorum|the Quorum]] and pass through it into [[Sigzil Haight]]'s demesne to find the lost soul the door spoke of.
- {863ag} In the demesne the delvers free the [[Voice of Many]], a [[Hearts|Heart]] made by Sigzil Haight, and hold its chamber for a minute while it restores its magic. The [[Keeper of Chains]] is driven off, and the Voice of Many carries the party back to [[Org/The Scale/index|the Scale]]'s stronghold on Færrin.
- {863ag} In [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], forty-eight people are found over three weeks as dried-up husks in their beds, dying overnight with peaceful faces. There is no pattern to the victims or the timing, and the first is [[Herald Vanderbloom]], a poor relation of the famous Vanderbloom family.
- {863ag} The [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/index|Magical Crimes Convox]] learns that Vanderbloom met, a day before he died, with a person in a strange burlap tunic who had arrived that day by train from the east. The only possible origin of that train is [[Geography/Calaria/Wrenford|Wrenford]]. Three convox investigators are sent to the town: [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Mickey Ironroots|Mickey Ironroots]], [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Cedric Corot|Cedric Corot]], and [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Krod Snodman|Krod Snodman]].
- {863ag} In the [[Geography/Calaria/Wrenford Commune|Wrenford commune]], the investigators learn that [[People/Lyric Burke|Lyric Burke]] left six months ago on a pilgrimage into the [[Verdant Expanse]] and never returned, and that a man fitting his description appeared in Hallia about three weeks ago, met a stranger, and vanished. Under his pillow they find a [[Phenomena/Feyrock|Feyrock]] carved as a leaf, which pulls toward the forest. Following it, they fight [[Bestiary/Deadly Mantis|deadly mantises]] and press on into the mid-boughs, where they come upon a child in a clearing, caught by the ankle in a tree branch.
- {863ag} The investigators free a boy, [[People/Tommy Lagerman|Tommy Lagerman]], from a branch that holds his ankle in the [[Verdant Expanse]], and bring him along. He says he is from [[Geography/Calaria/Wrenford|Wrenford]], was dared into the forest by a friend, wears a faint rainbow raiment of the [[Iridescent Host|Host]], and is unafraid of the dark.
- {863ag} Deeper in, the investigators meet a [[Bestiary/Verdant Court Fey|court of fey]] in a dark glade, led by [[People/Oriel|Oriel]] and [[People/Jin|Jin]]. The court offers to end the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] curse if the investigators entreat their Lady, or to point the curse at targets of their choosing instead. The investigators refuse the door and kill the fey. The curse continues; another person dies while they return.
- {863ag} The investigators bring [[People/Tommy Lagerman|Tommy Lagerman]] back and return him to his mother, [[People/Karen Lagerman|Karen Lagerman]], who lies to them about her work.
- {863ag} The [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/index|Magical Crimes Convox]] investigators take their only remaining lead, [[People/Lyric Burke|Lyric Burke]]'s [[Phenomena/Feyrock|Feyrock]] necklace, to [[Org/Crystal's Rock|Crystal's Rock]], a jewelers' conference in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]. They learn the stone is sold only to the wealthy, and that [[Org/Guren and Guren/People/Amos Guren|Amos Guren]] lately bought a piece from a bandaged man in a black raiment.
- {863ag} Following the black raiment into the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Gullet/index|Gullet]], the investigators find [[People/Anthony|Anthony]], the man who sold the stone, dead above a ritual circle in his apartment, half of one leg turned to Feyrock, which continues to grow. They take the leg and the [[Phenomena/Gloaming Codex|Gloaming Codex]] from the circle.
- {863ag} The investigators are drawn into the [[Phenomena/Gloaming Codex|Gloaming Codex]] when a sliver of Feyrock is pressed to a page. Inside the dark they are attacked by [[Bestiary/Carnivorous Ink|ink]] and [[Bestiary/Cursed Thought|cursed thoughts]], and choose to climb the stair deeper into the void.
- {863ag} The Party delivers the locked case to [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Diamond District/Crystal Hill|Crystal Hill]], a luxury apartment building in the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Diamond District/index|Diamond District]] whose lobby is a fane shaped like the inside of a gemstone. They are paid a thousand silver pieces and told [[Org/Sableclutch Scrap/index|Copperjaw]] will have more work.
- {863ag} Argyle reports to [[Org/The Scale/People/Dame Quay|Dame Quay]] at a [[Org/The Scale/index|Scale]] Pactbroker office, naming the [[Ugathal]] that ambushed them. Dame Quay offers to ask the [[Org/The Scale/index|Everchain]] after their like, and to send an information packet. Argyle calls the new signal the opposite of the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]], a starward song.
- {863ag} [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs]] and [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Anouk]] identify the stolen radar dish as the work of [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]], a small company founded months ago with no owner on file whose headquarters is a P.O. Box at a [[Org/Gryphonline/index|Gryphonline]] distribution center. The dish's signal comes from that same center.
- {863ag} The Party finds the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|The Crowded Flea]]. Its bouncer, a hairy man in a round hat, names himself Johnny too. [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/People/Shannon Soul|Shannon Soul]] pours Raylish gin and drinks in the party's toast to [[Geography/Raelion/index|Raelion]].
- {863ag} Johnny approaches the gang's table. The half-giant who holds court there says that if [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]] thinks him interesting, Johnny may find him the next evening at six on [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Pier 54|Pier 54]].
- {863ag} A clear night turns to a downpour that does not stop. Local diviners say the weather will hold until the [[Org/The Sears/index|Sears]] can find what is wrong with their oracular device, and the party wonders whether the [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Zorbon|Zorbon]] is behind it.
- {863ag} The next day the Party drives to the [[Org/Gryphonline/index|Gryphonline]] distribution center and stakes out Embercall's P.O. Box, while [[People/Othello|Othello]] hides in the rafters above. After three hours nothing has happened, and the watch continues.
- {863ag} Staked out in the day tripper outside the [[Org/Gryphonline/index|Gryphonline]] distribution center, the Party hears the five o'clock broadcast of [[The Situation Room]]. The [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/index|Magical Crimes Convox]]'s deputy director, Major-Chaplain [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Ewan McFoster|Ewan McFoster]], blames the endless rain on illegal augury, and says the convox is hunting whoever is responsible. No one comes for Embercall's P.O. Box all day. With their meeting with [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]] on [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Pier 54|Pier 54]] an hour away, Johnny and Benny walk into the mail office to break the box open while the others wait in the car.
- {863ag} The night before, Anzu spent an evening studying the [[Phenomena/Sentience Distributor|sentience distributor]] and Johnny tried to work it against the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]], learning the song lives only in a listener's head with nothing outside to touch.
- {863ag} In the morning [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Illmari Vaino|Illmari]] hands the Party two faxes. One, from [[Org/The Scale/People/Dame Quay|Dame Quay]], is a dossier on the [[Ugathal]]; it names the cryptozoologist [[People/Alfie Gallagher|Alfie Gallagher]] as the consultant the [[Org/The Scale/index|Scale]] uses in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]. The other, signed [[Org/Ghosts of Raelion|Hale]], reads only "Anchor and some interesting folks." Johnny calls Red on a chess-piece necklace; Red says Donovan has been asking questions and that the Party has kicked a hornet's nest.
- {863ag} The Party drives out of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]] for the first time, through the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Stepwell/index|Stepwell]] to the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Aurideon/index|Aurideon]], whose crystal dome now sheds the endless rain. They queue an hour to be let in and find the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/index|Magical Crimes Convox]] at 33 Rook's Crossing.
- {863ag} Detective [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Detective Ellis Brooks|Ellis Brooks]] takes the Party on as consultants at one gold a day and offers five hundred gold for [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]] brought in or killed. He shares what the convox knows: the rain is a corrective measure against illegal [[Phenomena/Augury|augury]], the augurs worked from the sewers until the flood drove them out, and the [[Bestiary/Auger|augers]] in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]] belong to the [[Org/Opaline Reserve|Opaline Reserve]]. Argyle matches the fire in the Party's shared dream, and the glow Tywelwyn gave off, to a white fire the convox ties to [[Org/Pyrelight/index|Pyrelight]].
- {863ag} The Party eats at the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Second Sun Diner|Second Sun Diner]], a family restaurant in Sableclutch whose rooftop dish was installed by the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]]. Argyle cuts the dish's wires and Anzu dents it. Johnny fakes a hair in his ice cream and talks a gift card out of the manager while Benny fails to slip into the back office. In the alley Benny feels a tingling like stepping into a [[Phenomena/Hearts|fane]], which fades away as the dish is spoiled.
- {863ag} With night falling the Party drives to a small open-air market in Widdershins that holds a way down into the sewers, where [[Org/Amber Call/People/Mr. Whiskers|Whiskers]] told them a [[The Zorbon|Zorbon]] meeting would be held. The rain has closed the market, and they park and get out.
- {863ag} The Party goes down the manhole at the open-air market in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]], past the honey seller [[People/Cora Honeysap|Cora Honeysap]], and into the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sewers|sewers]]. In a hideout further along they find the [[Anti-Zorbon Taskforce|Anti-Zorbon Taskforce]] slaughtered: enough blood for six or seven people, no bodies, no sign of a struggle, and [[Org/Amber Call/People/Mr. Whiskers|Whiskers']] belongings left behind. Something strong and clever ripped the people apart and carried the bodies off downriver.
- {863ag} Two robed spellcasters and three pale hunched creatures come upon the hideout afterward, searching it. The Party kills the spellcasters and two of the creatures; the third escapes. The dead carry corked vials of black [[Phenomena/Oil of Unlife|oil of unlife]] and false back teeth holding clear [[Phenomena/Mythotoxin|mythotoxin]]. Their raiments of the [[Iridescent Host|Host]] do not match standard Iridescent Church iconography.
- {863ag} The Party takes a boat down the underground river to a wide cavern where the water plunges out of sight; they cross a ledge around the central pit where Anzu nearly falls, and reach a lift and staging area built into the rock. A two-hundred-foot ladder climbs from the platform to an iron hatch that opens back into another stretch of sewers.
- {863ag} The Party rides the lift fifteen minutes down into the dark. Argyle feels his bond with the [[Judge of Ages|Judge]] grow faint. In a glowing cavern below, two giant [[Bestiary/Cave Serpent|serpents]] demand to know who they are and ask to see a permission slip, then attack.
- {863ag} The Party kills both giant [[Bestiary/Cave Serpent|serpents]]. Johnny skins enough hide for a pair of trousers, and they leave the poisonous algae in the snakes' water alone. As they make to leave, four more serpents rise from the pools; they pass them by and walk on.
- {863ag} Past the serpent clearing the cave narrows and the Party crosses a barrier, all their hairs standing on end, a clear sign of a [[Phenomena/Hearts|fane]]. Beyond it a grassy plain opens under an artificial sky, a thunderstorm with red lightning moving through it, the presence of the [[Eternal Pulse|Pulse]].
- {863ag} In the middle of the plain stands [[Nos Mortem]], a two-story wooden manor with a river running past its back porch into a dock. The skeleton majordomo [[Ossain Madrun]] meets them at the door, takes them for the guests Master Grayson said would arrive, and lets them in out of the wind.
- {863ag} The foyer has black and white checkered floors, marble walls, and pedestals holding vases and sculpture made of a matte white substance. Three ghosts in maid uniforms dust the foyer as the majordomo leads the Party to a lounge in the east wing.
- {863ag} The majordomo says Master Grayson is out on business, gives them a bell to ring for the footman [[Syrin]], and leaves. The bell has no tongue. The reeking ghoul footman answers and brings a decorative shield and a platter of pigs in blankets.
- {863ag} The ghost butler [[Salo Murn]] appears behind them in the Eastern Hall and tells them the manor is theirs except for the doorway to the basement in the Western Hall.
- {863ag} The Party explores as they wait. In the kitchen ghostly chefs prepare a meal and humanoid meat hangs to drain. Behind the house an enclosed greenhouse holds fruit trees with smooth pale barkless trunks and heavy deep red fruit.
- {863ag} In the master bedroom they find a large painting of Grayson holding a scalpel and a skull. The painting hangs on hinges, and behind it a door opens into a two-story private study. On its lower floor a runic circle is gouged into the boards and filled with dried blood, and within it lies the upper half of [[Mr. Whiskers]].
- {863ag} Anzu reads the circle as a lichdom ritual that draws the last life out of a corpse instead of needing a living victim, of a kind he knows from [[Belvedere]]. The Party takes Grayson's journal and books from the shelves and flees.
- {863ag} Grayson's journal, in neat handwriting, records his experiments at replacing a person's motivations while leaving the personality intact. Its second-to-last entry calls the "idiot deer" two-timing for setting up radar dishes after their agreement. Its last entry, dated that day, says two inquisitors were sniffing around Base B and that he will pack up and move.
- {863ag} The Party leaves the manor, runs back through the cavern past the dead serpents, and rides the elevator and ladder up into the rain of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]]. They drive to the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/index|Magical Crimes Convox]] to find [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Detective Ellis Brooks|Detective Brooks]].
- {863ag} The Party lays [[Org/Amber Call/People/Benjamin Grayson|Grayson]]'s journal on the desk of [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Detective Ellis Brooks|Detective Brooks]] at the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/index|Magical Crimes Convox]]. Brooks reads a page, sees whose it is, and hands it back: Grayson heads [[Org/Amber Call/index|Amber Call]] and sits on the council that rules [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]], and an investigation into a man like that would put Brooks's neck and the Party's on the line. He wants nothing to do with it.
- {863ag} The Party trades the gems taken from [[Org/Amber Call/People/Benjamin Grayson|Grayson]]'s study for coin at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Ledger, Ledger, and Light|Ledger, Ledger, and Light]], a bank in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]'s financial district, and opens an account. They buy gear from [[Org/The Undertable/People/Smiler|Smiler]] at [[Org/The Undertable/index|the Undertable]].
- {863ag} Back at the [[Sin and Tonic]], [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Anouk]] laces the snakeskin the Party took from the [[Bestiary/Cave Serpent|cave serpents]] onto Argyle's shield, drawn taut enough to stiffen the face.
- {863ag} The Party stakes out [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|the Crowded Flea]] and counts eight [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhats]] going in over the busiest hour and none coming out. Every gang member they can pick out has something of an animal about him on top of human stock.
- {863ag} At three in the morning the Party teleports into the gang's back room at the Crowded Flea and finds more of them than the street showed. The gang are werecreatures, turning into boars, rats and a crocodile, and [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]], the half-giant who speaks for them, fights with his fists.
- {863ag} The fight turns against the Party. Benny, Argyle and Johnny are killed. Anzu escapes through the window, runs out along the piers, and loses them.
- {863ag} Anzu runs from the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|Crowded Flea]] through the rain-soaked alleys to the [[Sin and Tonic]], reaching it around four in the morning. He tells himself that it is a test, that they stay, and sleeps until near noon.
- {863ag} Johnny and Benny die in the gang's back room and wake before [[Aut]] in the empty place between [[Færrin]] and the [[Godhome]]. Aut tells them that the dead of Færrin pass into the [[Pharos]] and float up to the Godhome, the only way there, and that Argyle has already gone ahead of them. He will not let them into the Pharos from where they are, and pushes them back to where they died; each of them leaves a piece of himself behind, whole but unable to grow. He marks each of them with three blue dots in a triangle, which they can show or hide at will and which reveals itself to anyone who has already seen it, and asks them to greet his friends at 13 Bright Street.
- {863ag} Johnny and Benny wake in the river outside the tavern, stripped to their underwear, and swim to shore. They walk back the long way, holding a morning funeral for Argyle on the riverbank; Johnny plays a dirge and lets the body drift downstream, and Benny vows to kill the half-giant [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]] to honor him.
- {863ag} Anzu comes out into the bar to find Illmari talking with a polar bear in a trench coat and hat: [[People/Sir Arctos|Sir Arctos]], a new member of [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]]. Illmari tells him the gang will not come into the tavern, and that the danger outside is no worse than it was before.
- {863ag} Johnny and Benny reach the Sin and Tonic at the same time, and Sir Arctos heals their wounds. Johnny takes back his sunglasses from Anzu and tells them Argyle did not make it. He says the being that put them back together predicts everything and could not predict them, which he thinks is because of the [[Voidsong]].
- {863ag} That night all of them dream of Argyle chained: his left wrist and ankle in wrought iron shackles engraved with red runes, drawn down out of sight, and his right wrist and ankle in shining golden shackles, drawn upward.
- {863ag} In the morning the four of them take a taxi into the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Aurideon/index|Aurideon]], where a massive concrete tower has risen through the crystal dome, one that only Johnny and Benny can see. At 13 Bright Street they find the office of the [[Org/Friends of Aut|Friends of Aut]]: a reception hall hung with portraits of raimented figures of many faiths, a black stone seal in the floor set with three blue sapphires in the shape of Aut's mark, and a dwarven woman at the desk who calls for the guide Silas.
- {863ag} Silas leads them up to the threshold room, where a shelf of [[Phenomena/Voice Box|voice boxes]] waits, and hands them a week-old report that warns of shadows and tells them to keep their box on them. He says the [[Pharos]] is ritualistic and follows the Rule of Three, and tells them to knock three times on the black doorway. They take a voice box, which does not resonate, and Johnny knocks: the lights go out, return with the pressure of the ocean floor, then go out again and leave them elsewhere.
- {863ag} They arrive by night in a silent, rain-soaked plaza in the [[Geography/Black and White/Plaza|Black and White]], a city they do not know. Four buildings face the square: Save Your Soul Incorporated, boarded and half collapsed, with three speakers on poles; the Soundscape Theaters, boarded, with one; the Horizon Gate Hotel, boarded, with one; and Vermillion Square Station, a stair down to an underground tram station, the only way not closed. None of them can sense a soul.
- {863ag} In Vermillion Square Station a tram stands with its front against a tunnel and a moth a foot across rests in the driver's cab, its wings making a piano's sound. The voice box grows warm near it. Johnny guesses they must catch the moth in the box, use it to open one of the closed buildings, and take a sound from each until they have three for Save Your Soul Incorporated; a board pulled from the hotel door springs back into place with a shriek.
}

- {863ag} In Vermillion Square Station Johnny shatters the front of the tram with needle darts, and Benny catches the moth in the [[Phenomena/Voice Box|voice box]] as it flies out. The moth bursts into a cloud of scales, the box plays a faint piano melody, and a light comes on.
- {863ag} They pour the caught sound into the speaker outside the [[Geography/Black and White/Soundscape Theaters|Soundscape Theaters]], and the cinema returns to its working state: fresh paint, a revolving door, a lobby of concession stands and film posters, and shades queuing at the ticket booth. The one film showing is *Song on Fire*, and its closing credits name Helena Ashcroft as the Spark, [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn Leatherhide]] as the Kindling, Elara Vance as the Antenna, and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]] as the Outer God.
- {863ag} Four of the shades in the audience carry the caught sound, and the Party fights them for it. The shades throw their own heads, have no bones, and break apart into moth scales when killed. Johnny's illusion of Argyle is disbelieved and stops affecting them.
- {863ag} They take the sound back out of the theater's speaker and carry it to the [[Geography/Black and White/Horizon Gate Hotel|Horizon Gate Hotel]], where it opens the doors. Inside, speakers set in the walls open one passage and seal another as sounds are moved between them, and the Party crosses rooms 101 to 103 and opens the front door again.
- {863ag} The shades of the [[Geography/Black and White/Plaza|plaza]] have grown opaque, and now and then one stands still and seems to face the Party before fading back into the crowd.
- {863ag} Three caught sounds clear the fallen roof of [[Geography/Black and White/Save Your Soul Incorporated|Save Your Soul Incorporated]]. Inside are a reception desk, shades at work, and an elevator whose buttons are engraved with symbols in place of numbers: the three wavy lines of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]], three dots in a triangle, a polyhedron, and a telescope. Only the three-dot button lights, and it carries them up into a white void of fog where [[Aut]] floats.
- {863ag} Aut calls back the pieces of Johnny and Benny left in the [[Pharos]] and both are whole again. He answers their questions: the [[Bestiary/Shade|shades]] are native to the [[Geography/Black and White/index|Black and White]] and the dead of [[Færrin]] do not linger there; [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] was built around the site where Aurelia first climbed to the [[Godhome]] by the Pharos; anyone who makes that trek and returns is a [[Hierophant|hierophant]], and a few are alive, among them Aurelia VII; [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]] has to do with the [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]], which is a derivative of the [[Voidsong]]; and the [[Phenomena/Firmament|firmament]] can be broken by destructive resonance, the same sound made inside and outside it and loud enough. He has watched them only since they heard the Voidsong, and cannot predict those who have, which is why [[Org/Amber Call/People/Benjamin Grayson|Master Grayson]] is a blank to him. He has friends in high places, more in [[Belvedere]] than in the Church, and the Pontifex does not approve of him.
- {863ag} Arctos asks for one of Aut's marks and takes it on his chest. Aut tells them [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]] is at 412 Anchor Boulevard in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]] with four guards, one of them [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]], and that Hlarf will be alone and drunk in an alley shortly after four in the morning, and gives them the address.
- {863ag} They try the elevator's button for the Host and it does not light. The three-dot button carries them to a concrete wall bearing a black stone threshold in the shape of a door, and three knocks return them to the Pharos.
- {863ag} The Party waits in the alley. Hlarf parks, gets out drunk to piss in a fountain, and they set on him. Johnny takes the car keys, curses him with an albatross, and terrifies him; Arctos heals Johnny and strikes him; Benny jumps from a low roof and flanks him; and [[People/Anzu|Anzu]], called Mindbird, pulls a piss-soaked coin from the fountain and sends it through Hlarf's head, killing him. They take his car, a 632 Chorath Aventine.

- {863ag} In the alley the Party loots [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]]'s body: a locked journal, a bank card from [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Iridite Mutual|Iridite Mutual]], and a keychain with two keys and the logo of a Gas-n-Go auto body shop. In his car they find a go-bag of clothes, fake IDs bearing Hlarf's picture under other names alongside other faces of the gang, a levered crowbar and a set of lockpicks, and no tracking device. They throw the body in the river and drive the car to the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Sin and Tonic|Sin and Tonic]], where [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Dura Oil-Drinker|Dura]] disarms the garage traps and pulls it in, paints it a cheap green, and swaps the day tripper's plates onto it.
- {863ag} At [[Org/The Undertable/index|the Undertable]], [[Smiler]] draws nine hundred gold from Hlarf's card and keeps fifty for the work, and silvers weapons for the Party. They buy matching ponchos to move through the rain unnoticed, and [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] buys each of them a potion of emergency escape. They cannot pick the journal's lock, and break a pick trying.
- {863ag} [[People/Benny|Benny]] and [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] scout 412 Anchor Boulevard in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]] and find a [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]] auto body shop. Their own car sits on a hoist in one of its three bays. They watch an hour and see a car leave, rain sizzling on its hot roof. That night they watch the shop: the employees lock up at eight, and around ten a car brings four Roundhats, who let themselves in the front door with a key.
- {863ag} The Party returns the next evening, enters by the service door with one of Hlarf's keys, and finds the store level empty. They take their car keys from a rack by the counter, and open the locked back door with the other key.
- {863ag} Beyond the door the shop gives way to a [[Hearts|Heart]]'s fane: a counterclockwise spiral stair between stained glass showing one unbroken fire, warm air, and steel plating that moves like breathing. The stair admits one at a time. Below, an ornate steel-and-glass hall leads to a glass bridge over a gap and a throne on a raised altar.
- {863ag} On the throne sits what is left of [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]]: a tall, hollow husk of black matter with flame burning where its chest and skull were, two black-stained antlers on its head, and a raiment of jet black where his simulacrum had worn the Host's. Roundhats stand with him, among them a boar, a rat and a tiger. The husk was no werecreature.
- {863ag} The Party crosses the bridge in their ponchos before they are seen. The rat raises the alarm, and the boar charges Arctos, saying it had killed him before. [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] strips the magic from the black cape that fights at Tywelwyn's shoulder, and the Party kills the boar, the rat and the tiger. Tywelwyn throws fire and bolts of divine light; when Benny's pick wounds the husk, the fire inside it bursts out over him and Arctos.
- {863ag} [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] takes hold of Tywelwyn's mind and makes it drive his body to move. The husk cannot move, and its muscles tear themselves apart. It collapses to the ground, and the Roundhat Gang is ended.
- {863ag} Past the throne the Party finds a seven-sided antechamber below the fane, with a door in each of its six outer walls and a five-foot chunk of obsidian floating and turning over its center. Veins of stained glass run through the rock and spread into its cracks as they watch.
- {863ag} A voice comes out of the obsidian. It calls itself the iron gauntlet in a glass glove, says it is the veins within the rock and not the rock itself, and greets the Party as the Poncho Boys and as the ones who murdered [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]].
- {863ag} The Heart says [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]] made it, but will not say how, only that anyone could with the right recipe. It names the six gods on the doors as its own, inherited from him: [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Giant|Giant]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/War|War]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Esoterica]] and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Regent|Regent]]. The gods come from a Godhome and want to visit their blessings on [[Færrin]]: eternal fire, torment, and a clean slate. Killing Tywelwyn has held off their coming for a while, and they are not here now. The [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]] is for Pyre, and Pyre told Tywelwyn how to make a Heart.
- {863ag} Behind Pyre is Tywelwyn’s bedroom, behind Herald the armory, behind Giant the radar dish plant and the place he prepared for the pilgrimage, behind War his office, behind Esoterica a haberdasher and behind Regent an orrery. The Heart will not spring the fane’s traps on the Party now that Johnny has convinced it that Tywelwyn attacked first and they own it.
- {863ag} In the armory the Party recovers the gear taken from their dead bodies, and finds a hardened case holding a white armband and a ring box holding two silver rings, one with an orange gem and one with a blue. They take [[People/Argyle|Argyle]]’s axe, shield, grappling gun and gold as well.
- {863ag} In Tywelwyn’s office they find a typewriter, chalkboards, and a map of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] with points circled, and next to them sheet music and harmonies pointing at the same points. His notes are about resonance: vibrating one thing to make another answer at the same frequency, and the destructive energy when two such pulses meet. An occult reading shows the scheme: spread a harmony through Hallia so the city vibrates at the same frequency as something far away, and let that thing come to Hallia. The radar dishes are doing it, with a hierarchy in which dishes across Sableclutch point at the [[Org/Gryphonline/index|Gryphonline]] distribution center, which in turn points at a spot within [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]].
- {863ag} Amid the office papers are records for the Gas-n-Go and two other franchises, the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|Crowded Flea]], two laundromats, a churro restaurant and a fried chicken restaurant, with ledgers showing money made against money reported. Two notebooks are tucked under the rest. One details the radar dish work, its timelines, complaints that materials arrive too slowly, and directions to [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]], and notes that [[Org/Amber Call/People/Benjamin Grayson|Grayson]] had lately been looking into the dish supply. The other logs about thirty failed augury attempts, numbered, the most recent about a week before with a one beside it, on the day the Party went looking for Flynn; none are dated after the Party’s first day on the job.
- {863ag} At ten that night a car brings the shift crew of werecreatures to the shop, raising the garage shutters and heading for the basement. The Party ambushes them at the door: a bear, a crocodile and a bat, all in round hats. The bear swells to fill the hall when wounded and pins Arctos against a wall. The Party kills the crocodile and the bear, and Benny runs down the bat as it flees to its car.
- {863ag- {863ag} The Party drives the gang's cars and their recovered company car back to the [[Sin and Tonic]], where [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Dura Oil-Drinker|Dura]] is getting ready for bed. The rain has stopped for the first time in more than a week, though the sky stays overcast. They return the company car and keep the gang's.
- {863ag} They decide to sell both stolen cars and buy a legal one, park the two in the garage out of sight, and drive to the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/index|Magical Crimes Convox]] in the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Aurideon/index|Aurideon]] to turn in the bounty on [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]]. The desk tells them that [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Detective Ellis Brooks|Brooks]] has resigned and is no longer with the agency, and pays them what they are owed.
- {863ag} Around two in the morning the Party goes to the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/index|Inquisition]]'s office and asks for [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/People/Inquisitor Penitence|Penitence]] or Absolution, the two [[Aut]] named. Brother Zeal rouses Penitence, who takes them to a questioning room whose bell rings whenever a true thing is said, and hears their account of the fane beneath the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]], the radar dishes, and [[Org/Amber Call/People/Benjamin Grayson|Grayson]]. They leave out the cards they took, their deaths in the fane, [[Aut]], and the invitation to the pilgrimage. Penitence says the Inquisition will take the matter from there, asks for the radar dish, which the Party leaves behind the bar, and pays them 125 gold as a gesture of goodwill. He refuses to carry word of it to anyone outside the Inquisition.
- {863ag} The Party sleeps until the afternoon, and wakes to find the radar dish gone: two Inquisitors came to the bar, asked after its licensing, and took the dish away. Before sleeping, [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] reached out to the singer of the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] and promised to save them, and the song quickened for half a second. [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] prayed to the [[Iridescent Host|Host]] and asked why he had been awakened. [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] drank until sunrise and told whoever was watching that he knew, and got no answer.
- {863ag} They drive both stolen cars to [[Org/The Undertable/People/Smiler|Smiler]] at [[Org/The Undertable/index|the Undertable]]. He says fencing cars is not his usual trade but agrees to put out feelers: he can almost certainly find a buyer for the minivan, but the luxury Aventine draws too much attention and he will only look for someone to swap its registration. He will not keep the cars at the shop, so the Party drives them home.
- {863ag} They drive past the Gas-n-Go and find it shuttered in the middle of the day with a crowd outside; Inquisitors work inside the store level and have left the door down into the fane standing open. There is no blood for them to find.
- {863ag} No one answers at Brooks's fifth-floor flat in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Prism Heights/index|Prism Heights]], and [[People/Benny|Benny]] picks the lock. Inside are case files he had brought home, none of them about Tywelwyn or Grayson, a spray of blood across the wall by the bed with three faint, almost parallel grooves cut through it, and a trail of blood leading to the window. The claw marks are too big to belong to what they fought, and there is not blood enough to say Brooks died there. He was rent-poor and kept nothing of value.
- {863ag} [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] throws silver needle darts at the empty air by the window, and a hidden [[Bestiary/Cairn White|cairn white]] and two [[Bestiary/Lovelorn|lovelorn]] set on the Party. The cairn white drains [[People/Benny|Benny]] and knocks him and Johnny down before it is destroyed, and a lovelorn latches onto [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]]'s face until he knocks it off. Arctos heals the others back up. A third creature skitters away, and the Party wipes their fingerprints from the room and leaves. Arctos casts [[Phenomena/Augury|augury]] on whether to go after Brooks and sees the four of them as zombies, and they decide to let him go.
- {863ag} Back at the Sin and Tonic, Ginny hands them a fax from [[Org/The Undertable/People/Smiler|Smiler]]: he has found someone willing to pay 3,200 for the minivan and gives an address to drop it off that night. The Party takes it for a trap.
- {863ag} They drive the crew's car into the shop, giving the Party three cars in all, and spend the rest of the night loading papers out of the office. They mean to report the radar scheme to the authorities and collect the bounty on Tywelwyn first, and talk of asking [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Illmari Vaino|Illmari]] for a lawyer to claim the dead man's businesses.
- {863ag} The Party spends the evening at the [[Sin and Tonic]]. [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] buys heal scrolls and [[People/Benny|Benny]] and [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] healing potions, Johnny drinks coffee to stay awake, and [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] visits a small [[Iridescent Host|Host]] church near the bar to network with its priest, who keeps the church's single prayer engine.
- {863ag} At midnight the Party drives the stolen minivan and [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Dura Oil-Drinker|Dura]]'s company car to an abandoned parking lot in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]]. Three members of the [[Org/Velvet Mark/index|Velvet Mark]] arrive to meet them, all wearing ravens of the [[Iridescent Host|Host]]: a human driver, a second henchman, and an older dwarf who runs the deal. Johnny gives the alias Jonathan Skyfall and says the minivan came from [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]], whose gang is dead and whose turf is free.
- {863ag} The dwarf has the van inspected and, satisfied, pays 3,200 gold in a briefcase. Anzu checks the money and the Party hands over the keys. Arctos tries to sell the Velvet Mark the Aventine too; the dwarf refuses. One henchman leaves the Party a card for the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Masque District/Crystal Globe|Crystal Globe]] and tells them to say Cosimo sent them.
- {863ag} Back at the bar the Party pays [[Org/The Undertable/People/Smiler|Smiler]] 3,000 to make the black Aventine street legal. He registers it under Arctos as a car totaled and repaired, has it repainted matte black, and holds it a day. Johnny has a stolen suit tailored and adds a shoulder perch for a bird, Arctos buys healer's gloves from Smiler, and Benny buys a rapier. Johnny speaks to [[Org/Ghosts of Raelion|Red]] through his pond piece and asks him to arrange a word with Donnie.
- {863ag} Two mornings later [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Anouk]] asks the Party for help. Her brother [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs]] went out about two days earlier following a promising lead on the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] and has not returned. She gives them a scrap of paper in his handwriting with an address in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]], at void 26, and offers to try to open the locked journal the Party took from [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]].
- {863ag} The Party picks up the Aventine and slips voidward down the [[Phenomena/Infinite Horizon|horizon]]. At void 26, Sableclutch thins into frontier: dirt roads, cheap tenements, log cabins, a half-chopped forest, and a river the locals dump their waste into. One step further voidward lies the first [[Phenomena/Joker World|Joker World]] on the horizon that way, a world under constant blood rain, and [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] ends there.
- {863ag} The address is a one-room log bungalow with an A-frame roof, a small cooking area and no bathroom, set up like a hiker's rest stop. A faint buzz of magic cuts out as the Party enters. Inside, Anaïs is chained to a metal cot, his hands shackled to the headboard and a metal band locked over his mouth. [[Aut]]'s symbol, three blue dots in a triangle, hangs above the threshold.
- {863ag} Anaïs takes them for Aut's spies and kicks Anzu across the room. They unbolt the bedposts from the floor with a polytool and take the shackle and gag. The shackles open at a thought for Arctos, Benny and Johnny, who carry Aut's mark, but not for Anzu.
- {863ag} Calmed, Anaïs says he heard a [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/index|convox]] sensor report a blip with the same harmonics as the Voidsong, went to investigate, and was caught. The blip was a lure, and he believes a friend of Aut's in the church set it for someone listening in.
- {863ag} Anaïs explains that Aut and his siblings are not gods but the archetypal parts of a story. Aut, the Writer, designs the path he thinks the story should take; [[Divinity/The Narrative/Renge|Renge]], the Fickle Mistress, is the things that might happen instead; [[Divinity/The Narrative/Petr|Petr]] is the Threshold; [[Divinity/The Narrative/Insuperlex|Insuperlex]] is the Mountain; [[Divinity/The Narrative/Menhir|the Menhir]] is the Heroes. Aut and Renge are at odds, as are Insuperlex and the Menhir, and the siblings work together only when they must. No leader of a real Org is a friend to any of them.
- {863ag} Anaïs blames Aut for the current prime minister, for [[Geography/Raelion/index|Raelion]]'s destruction, for [[Geography/Brithwyn/index|Brithwyn]] breaking from [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]], for Aurthalaxus the Plaguebearer killing close to half of [[Færrin]]'s people some two hundred years ago, and possibly for [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] itself. He says Renge helped slay [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the Deep]], a god that once threatened the world, and tried and failed to stop the assassination of the previous prime minister.
- {863ag} The Party tells him of six gods coming to destroy the world. He recognized [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Giant|Giant]] from Renge's talk, but had never heard of [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Regent|Regent]] or [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Esoterica]].
- {863ag} Anaïs and Anouk offer to attend the gathering on Saturday separately and meet the Party there. The invitation the Party stole names no one and is plain card stock with gold in common. Anaïs threatens to kill them if they sell the twins out to Aut. He has been 35 for nine months and will be 36 in three months, says he is made of skin though a hard armoured thing sits behind his head where a skull would be, and has not spoken with Renge in years.
- {863ag} With two days before the pilgrimage, the Party prepares in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]. They shop at [[Org/Concordia|Concordia]] for a plain suit for [[People/Benny|Benny]], nondescript medium armor for [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] to wear in place of his own, paper, gold ink and enough black hair dye for a bear, and a corduroy jacket for [[People/Anzu|Anzu]]. Arctos buys a half plate from [[Org/The Undertable/People/Smiler|Smiler]].
- {863ag} [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] forges three more invitations from the stolen one, matching its blue cardstock and gold ink closely enough that the real one could not be told from the copies. They dye [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] black and fit him with a collar so he can pass as someone's pet black bear, though he is far too large for one.
- {863ag} [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs]] and [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Anouk]] now hold the address from the invitation and mean to find their own way into the gathering rather than use a copy. Asked to forge copies, they decline, neither being any good at it. The Party reasons the gathering is likely connected to [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]].
- {863ag} [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Anouk]] has broken the arcane lock on the journal the Party took from [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]] and hands it back. It proves to be Hlarf's own diary, three months of daily entries, recording coins he skimmed from the Roundhat rackets before they reached the gang and some competent poems. In an entry from two months before he mentions driving through the ring into [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]] to meet someone, which tells the Party that people can still pass through the border there.
- {863ag} In the downtime [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] returns to the small [[Iridescent Host|Host]] church near the [[Sin and Tonic]] and works to make himself a known quantity there, angling to become a guest preacher, and [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] spends his days at the [[Sin and Tonic]] helping the [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] members with their work.
- {863ag} The Party drives the Aventine out of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] toward the gathering, a little under a day's travel. Low on gas, they stop at a rundown rest-stop station with two pumps and kinked hoses. The cashier is an older human man with a small raiment of the [[Iridescent Host|Host]], who charges two silver for a fill and tries to sell them homemade pills. He asks them to wait while he checks their money, working a marker over their coins behind the counter.
- {863ag} [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] finds fresh tire tracks to a white van in the lot with no footprints leading from it, and a glint of a scope inside. He casts an illusion of a one-way mirror around the van. Four robbers come out, a well-dressed masked man who sees through the illusion and three more with odd guns: pistols that fire blue bolts of light, and a long gun that launches a slug through Johnny's chest. The Party kills them, and the cashier, who was in on it, is knocked out and tied up.
- {863ag} The Party searches the van and the bodies. Each of the four robbers carried a token stamped with an S crossed by a rifle, the mark of the firearms maker [[Org/Sable and Suns/index|Sable and Suns]], and the surviving robber says they bought the guns from a man named Lark in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], in a neighborhood called [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Deosil|Deosil]], and that this was the fourth or fifth time they had robbed travelers at the station. They take a railgun and three plasma rifles and about 135 gold, fill jerry cans with gasoline from the pumps, and leave the robbers' van and the cashier's car behind.
- {863ag} They drive on. The suns set and an aurora hangs over [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]], still the [[Iridescent Host|Host]]'s land. Spotlights point up from a town that should be dead, and in its center an Istrian strider stands under construction, a platform on eight legs with buildings on top.
- {863ag} The town is [[Geography/Calaria/Ragged Roost|Ragged Roost]], an abandoned mining town whose sign reads a population scribbled out to zero. The pilgrimage fills its main street with fairy lights, banners reading "Pilgrimage Welcome," tables of hors d'oeuvres and champagne, and hundreds of guests in masks, some with armed attendants. Crossing the town line flattens every raiment to the same plain gray. Signs direct cars to a parking lot and a line of guests having their invitations checked and being handed masks. The Party parks and joins the line.
- {863ag} The Party joins the line at [[Geography/Calaria/Ragged Roost|Ragged Roost]]. The parking lot holds some 250 cars of every kind, cheap daily drivers beside luxury cars and unmarked black cars, carrying the marks of [[Org/Prime Meridian/index|Prime Meridian]], [[Org/Concordia|Concordia]], the [[Org/Hildebrandt Corporation/index|Hildebrandt Corporation]], [[Org/Hollowpact]], the [[Org/Velvet Mark/index|Velvet Mark]] and the [[Org/Mask Makers|Mask Makers]].
- {863ag} Two [[Org/The Harlequins/index|Harlequins]] in red and green pinstripes take the stack of four invitations and hand out plain white masks that press to any face. [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] takes a dragon, [[People/Benny|Benny]] a gorilla, [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] a blank mask and [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] a two-faced theater mask to wear under his sunglasses.
- {863ag} The main street offers a fortune teller, a barker before a rainbow prism, a Harlequin with a painter's palette before blank wooden mannequins, a table of dice and poker chips, and two signposted paths out of town, one marked with a fairy ring of mushrooms and one with crossed swords.
- {863ag} The host of the pilgrimage stands on the scaffolding of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]] and addresses the crowd: a tall lanky figure, plainly not human, in a black pinstriped suit and a plain white mask with crescent eyes and a wide black grin. He means to take them on his pilgrimage to the Void Side Wall aboard the strider he and his Istrian companions are building, and to cull the some four hundred guests he sets them the [[Phenomena/Keystone|keystones]]: twenty cut gems, one in his hand and nineteen hidden in or around [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], each buying passage for one vehicle. He cares nothing for how a keystone is gotten, he says, only that it be in hand when the strider leaves in six months. He vanishes in a flash of smoke.
- {863ag} As the crowd scatters, [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] resonates and finds some forty people among the guests who have heard the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]].
- {863ag} The Party splits. [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] and [[People/Benny|Benny]] take the crossed-swords path to a disused train yard and a Harlequin's trial by combat, while [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] and [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] hold their place in the fortune teller's line until Johnny sends word it is gladiator combat.
- {863ag} At the trial the Harlequin spins a wheel of colors. Green summons three goat-like horned creatures that melt and kill a hired band of three in moments, and the Party's turn lands on red, summoning three [[Bestiary/Barbazu|Barbazu]] and a [[Bestiary/Brimorak|Brimorak]].
- {863ag} The Party wins the fight, most of them on the ground and bleeding before the end, and [[People/Benny|Benny]] kills the last devil. The crowd that watched has thinned, and the Harlequin strikes red from the wheel.
- {863ag} The Harlequin leads them to an emptied foreman's office and gives them three questions. They learn that the keystone nearest the [[Sin and Tonic]] is number 14, that it is held by a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] calling itself Rapid Connection, and that the man most likely to lead them to that Heart is [[People/Hogan Voss Darkmoor|Archmechanic Hogan Voss Darkmoor]] of the Darkmoors. The Harlequin will not give any keystone's location or cross streets, and drops through a trapdoor.
- {863ag} The Party means to take another hint from the party while it still runs.
- {863ag} The Party stays at the pilgrimage after its first questions are spent. [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] resonates among the waiting guests; most resonate back, though the armed attendants around the wealthier guests do not, and a pair ahead of him, a gnome and a taller elf, hold his gaze a beat longer than the rest.
- {863ag} On the fairy-ring path a Harlequin sets them an association game: three mushroom rings in a Venn diagram, one player to each, items to be placed in the overlaps that connect the players. The Party fills the four overlaps with a scroll of invisibility, a [[Org/Belvedere|Belvedere]] notebook, a three-dot mark [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] draws from [[Aut]]'s symbol, and one of [[People/Argyle|Argyle]]'s business cards. The machine stalls on the unknown symbol but passes them, and they are winner twelve of the evening.
- {863ag} Their question goes to keystone 14: its holder is a collector of fine art.
- {863ag} The fortune teller reads them a Harrow fortune, the Fool for the past, the World Tree inverted for a broken connection, the Hooded Man, and the Forest for the rising, and then gives a hint: the holder of keystone 14 collects paintings, oil or acrylic on canvas.
- {863ag} They split for the last games. [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] and [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] take the prism, seven colored walls around a key and seven potions to pass them, and work the order out from a riddle of colors; Anzu reaches through and pulls the key out. [[People/Benny|Benny]] and [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] take the dice table, where Benny bets fifty gold and cheats behind Johnny's distracting backflip, and wins a hundred.
- {863ag} They spend their last questions on keystone 15: the dice game says its holder would trade it for a relic of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]], a reliquary or a holy book, and the prism game names Second-Among-Equals [[People/Thistle Monroe|Thistle Monroe]] as the one most likely to knowingly lead them to it.
- {863ag} The Harlequins will say only that the key they won is for something important, and the Party keeps it along with their masks.
- {863ag} In the fortune line they fall in with the elf and gnome from the arena: [[Org/Protectorate/People/Tamara McKay|Tamara McKay]] of the [[Org/Protectorate/index|Protectorate]], born in [[Geography/Brithwyn/index|Brithwyn]], and her companion. The two fought ice creatures to the Party's fire, and are after keystone 8. Tamara declines an alliance and says the Protectorate will get its keystone.
- {863ag} The Party drives the eight hours home, resting in shifts, and reaches the [[Sin and Tonic]] at eight in the morning.
- {863ag} [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] calls [[Org/Ghosts of Raelion|Red]] through his chess piece and learns their contact at [[Org/Sable and Suns/index|Sable and Suns]] is [[Org/Sable and Suns/People/Lark Crowe|Lark Crowe]], and that Moonlight, an arms dealer, can be found in the market in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Deosil|Deosil]].
- {863ag} They drive into the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Aurideon/index|Aurideon]] to see Arctos's friend Minister [[People/Valerius Vane|Valerius Vane]], lose their way in the winding residential north, and are escorted to the Vane manor by church officers. The majordomo [[People/Crowley Hart|Crowley Hart]] says Vane was summoned to the council and shows them to the reading room, where a panorama of the Aurideon skyline has been painted over where the [[Pharos]] now stands.
- {863ag} The Vane family keeps no [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] in the house, holding that Hearts should not run all of society.
- {863ag} At the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Masque District/Belvedere Library|Belvedere library]] on the edge of the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Masque District/index|Masque District]], [[People/Anzu|Anzu]]'s membership gets the four of them in on day passes. Anzu reads up on Archmechanics, the engineers who supervise a city's transport cluster for [[Org/Prime Meridian/index|Prime Meridian]].
- {863ag} Searching for the two artist names, Anzu finds nothing for one and, for the other, a six-year-old clipping from a Vane family event naming the artist as one the Vane family patronized.
- {863ag} In the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Masque District/Belvedere Library|Belvedere library]], [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] and [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] spend three hours going through the periodicals while [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] and [[People/Benny|Benny]] work the reference shelves. The oldest mention of the [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]] is a little under two years old, some six months after the [[Voidsong]] was first heard, in the first reports of the wall of fire around [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]]: of the rescuers who passed through the flame, most never returned, and the few who were let back out spoke of the Embercall and died soon after.
- {863ag} The same papers explain the tower at the center of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]]. An aeronautics company began a skyscraper there to move its headquarters and renew the district, then folded when [[Org/Hildebrandt Corporation/index|Hildebrandt]] beat it out of the market, leaving the building unfinished. Six months after the fire closed the district, lights showed inside the tower as if it were being lived in. A few months after that an emissary came out through the cordon to say the people would be admitted to a party held inside by [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]], and music has been heard from the tower ever since, with an event held there about every other week. They also find a note of an Istrian strider that hummed a strange melody to itself and slipped away, two months ago.
- {863ag} They find no record of [[Org/Prime Meridian/Rapid Connection|Rapid Connection]], but learn that [[Org/Prime Meridian/index|Prime Meridian]] installed three great [[Phenomena/Hearts|Hearts]] to coordinate [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]'s transport about a century ago, one of them in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]].
- {863ag} [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] hears of a fan club of five in [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]], all now in prison for trying to break into Minister [[People/Valerius Vane|Vane]]'s home to meet him, who told the arresting officers they knew it was not his fault.
- {863ag} The Party returns to [[People/Valerius Vane|Vane]]'s manor and finds the minister still away at the council; [[People/Crowley Hart|Crowley]] takes a note asking him to call at Iconoclasm when he has time.
- {863ag} Back at the [[Sin and Tonic]] they find [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Anouk]] and [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs]] returned from the gathering. They mugged a guest for invitations, arrived late, and spent two questions on the keystone nearest the bar: it is number 14. Four parties hunt it in all, counting the twins and the Party; the other two are [[People/Sbrtlby Jotes|Sbrtlby Jotes]] and his hired henchmen, and Crawford Reeves and Louis Maller of [[Org/Concordia|Concordia]]. The twins mean to kill whoever takes it first.
- {863ag} The Party reports [[People/Argyle|Argyle]]'s death to [[Org/The Scale/index|the Scale]] by fax, naming gang violence.
- {863ag} That night a [[Org/Ghosts of Raelion|Ghost]] named [[People/Donnie|Donnie]] comes half-translucent into [[People/Johnny|Johnny]]'s room at the bar. He says the Ghosts have had a mole and that he has split the Raelish apart to find them, that Red cannot be reassigned and now works with him, and that the new firearms [[Org/Sable and Suns/index|Sable and Suns]] have begun making are the work of a consultant brought in from further down the horizon. He offers to ask around for a way into the Teller's Run party.
- {863ag} On Sunday the Party drives to the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus|Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus]], the building that runs [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]]'s trains, and asks at the gate for Rapid Connection. The guard's business is transport and he sends them off, but their car's radio turns itself to a dead frequency and a voice directs them around the back to a loading bay. There a servant of the Heart, wired with metal like the guard, asks how they know the name and what they have to sell. Johnny's talk of a painting goes badly, and they are put back on the street.
- {863ag} They resolve to visit the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Metropolitan Conservatory|Hallia Metropolitan Conservatory]] to learn what a painting worth trading to a Heart might be.
- {863ag} The Party drives to the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Metropolitan Conservatory|Hallia Metropolitan Conservatory]], the MetCon, the great glass museum over the river, to learn what a painting worth trading to a Heart might be. [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] charms the guide into talking about the works on show, among them Joker World by the contemporary painter [[People/Kellum Quinn|Kellum Quinn]], for sale at 64,000 gold, and the museum's one unsolved theft from about twenty years ago.
- {863ag} They return to [[People/Valerius Vane|Vane]]'s manor. The minister is still away at the council; [[People/Crowley Hart|Crowley]] lets [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] take the [[People/Kellum Quinn|Kellum Quinn]] landscape from the parlor, and Arctos adds two paintings of his own. All three go to the armory at [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]].
- {863ag} As they load the car Crowley brings out a paper faxed for Arctos reading Sbrtlby, 414 Anchor Street. The address is in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Deosil|Deosil]], sent by the [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Marchal]] twins.
- {863ag} At the factory the twins blow the side off the building and the Party takes the fleeing workers. [[People/Sbrtlby Jotes|Sbrtlby Jotes]] proves to be a [[Bestiary/Babau|babau]], a demon whose darkness blinds even dark-seeing eyes and whose spear leaves a wound that will not close. His hands are three [[Bestiary/Pusk|pusks]] and two [[Bestiary/Mioktan|mioktans]]. The Party kills them all, and Sbrtlby last, and is left to clean up the mess.
- {863ag} At the drug works the darkness lifts. The henchmen are dead, and [[People/Sbrtlby Jotes|Sbrtlby Jotes]] falls last, cut down by sword and bone and force. He is about four feet tall, red and mucus-covered, and looks the demon he is. On his body the Party finds a spear, a key ring holding four triangles of yellow paper, three vials of a thick yellow liquid, and a red choker. They leave, and the building folds in on itself behind them without touching anything around it. His soul is already remaking itself in the demons' [[Phenomena/Joker World|Joker world]], and ending him for good would mean going there.
- {863ag} In the rubble they find the [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Marchal]] twins unhurt inside a sphere that turned the falling building aside; the twins' own car was rammed into the works on the way in and is wrecked, so they ride back to the [[Sin and Tonic]] with the Party. They go off to rebuild their rocket hammers. [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] asks them for a radio tuned to a frequency he names, and they agree.
- {863ag} At the bar [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] reads what was taken off Sbrtlby: the four yellow triangles are fulus of concealment, set at the cardinal points of a fixed circle in which those inside go unseen by one chosen kind of creature; the vials are doses of an addiction suppressant; and the red choker is a choker of elocution, which lets its wearer speak the demons' tongue and goes to [[People/Johnny|Johnny]]. He cannot place the vials until the next morning.
- {863ag} The Party drives back to the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus|Sub Transit Nexus]] with the [[People/Kellum Quinn|Kellum Quinn]] *Second Meaning*, and this time the servant at the gate, Low-Mechanitor Exitum-ρ-15, looks the painting over and lets them in. Beyond the lobby the building is a warren of catwalks, pipes and silent wired workers, and [[People/Hogan Voss Darkmoor|Archmechanic Hogan Voss Darkmoor]] keeps a bare office on the second floor. He authenticates the Quinn, and when the Party says they have come for a keystone the mask goes quiet and [[Org/Prime Meridian/Rapid Connection|Rapid Connection]] speaks through it and agrees to see them.
- {863ag} Darkmoor takes them down a freight elevator into the Heart's fane: a ring of stone over thousands of gears of dull metal, each turning or reversing on its own. Rapid Connection has no mouth and speaks by grinding its gears into the sounds of speech. It offers gold, free transit, priority and shipping lights before it will part with the painting; the Party holds out for the keystone and promises it any art they find. [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] throws the painting into its central cortex, and the Heart strips the outer paint away to show the [[Pharos]] hidden under the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Aurideon/index|Aurideon]] skyline. It gives over keystone 14 in an ornate golden box and waives all Prime Meridian fees for the Party's travel, rail and road.
- {863ag} [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] reads the stone as a key to a sealed compartment of some kind, with something in it that only receives.
- {863ag} Coming back up into the lobby, they find [[Org/Concordia|Concordia]]: [[Org/Concordia/People/Crawford Reeves|Crawford Reeves]] and [[Org/Concordia/People/Louis Maller|Louis Maller]] with six Happy Time Enforcers, and the gatehouse outside already smoking. Reeves reads from a clipboard that under Concordia's charter the Party are happiness sinks and have five seconds to hand over all they own. The Archmechanic cannot fight as a civilian but drives the bodies of his workers, one of them firing a bolt of hot rebar down the lobby. Reeves is killed when the gear the Heart burned into his brow bursts, and [[People/Benny|Benny]] runs the clapping Maller through; the last enforcers fall as a blue light flashes from their eyes.
- {863ag} With Sbrtlby and both Concordia agents dead, the Party holds keystone 14 and no rival hunter is known to be left. The next thing tied to the keystone is six months away, and the Party means to spend the time shut in.
}
